      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-318601",
      ":question/problem": "Determine whether the following differential equation is exact:\n\n$$\n(1-s{e}^{rs})\\,\\text{d}r+(-r{e}^{rs}+4s)\\,\\text{d}s=0\n$$\n\nA differential equation of the form\n\n$$\nP(r,s)\\,\\text{d}r+Q(r,s)\\,\\text{d}s=0\n$$\n\nis exact if it satisfies the condition\n\n$$\n\\,{{field-1}},\n$$\n\nFor the equation $(1-s{e}^{rs})\\,\\text{d}r+(-r{e}^{rs}+4s)\\,\\text{d}s=0$, we have  \n\n$$\nP=\\,{{field-2}},\n$$\n\n$$\nQ=\\,{{field-3}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,  \n\n$$\n\\frac{\u2202P}{\u2202s}=\\,{{field-4}},\n$$\n\n$$\n\\frac{\u2202Q}{\u2202r}=\\,{{field-5}}.\n$$\n\nNow, since \n\n$$\n\\,{{field-6}},\n$$\n\n the equation {{field-7}}."
